            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0525" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365D.1163/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-12T19:00:00-05:00">October 12, 1939—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. Department’s instruction no. 513, July 19.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d582-f1"/>
                    Department is informed by Presbyterian Board of Foreign Missions that its
                    representatives in Ethiopia, Dr. John A. Cremer and the Reverend Duncan C.
                    Henry, have been expelled by the Italian authorities following expropriation of
                    mission property at Addis Ababa.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
